.TH CALC-QT 1 "October 2026" "calc-qt 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
calc-qt \- Windows Calculator engine with a native Qt interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calc-qt
[\fB\-\-type\fR \fIkeys\fR] [\fB\-\-screenshot\fR \fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Linux port of the open source Windows Calculator.
It has Standard, Scientific, Programmer and Date calculation modes,
history and memory.
The math is done by the upstream arbitrary precision engine.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-type " " \fIkeys\fR
Type \fIkeys\fR into the calculator once the window is up.
.TP
.BR \-\-screenshot " " \fIfile\fR
Save an image of the window to \fIfile\fR and quit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/calc-qt/calc-qt.conf
Mode, window position, theme and keep on top.
.SH NOTES
This is an unofficial build. It is not made or endorsed by Microsoft.
